# Runs before every push, so DS problems surface here — in your own terminal,
# inside the session that wrote the code — instead of in a review comment a day
# later. The same three checks run in CI, so a clean push is a green PR.
#
# The ratchet compares against your local origin/main, so `git fetch origin`
# occasionally keeps the baseline honest. It skips itself rather than blocking
# when it cannot read the base.
#
# To push anyway (a work-in-progress branch you want to share, or a finding you
# believe is a false positive — say so in the PR description):
#   git push --no-verify

npx tsc -b --noEmit || exit 1
npm run audit:tokens || exit 1
node scripts/audit-ratchet.cjs || exit 1
